beacond (1.4.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging. Two binary packages: beacond (the daemon,
    Architecture: any) and beacond-client (the beacon-status bash client,
    Architecture: all); the client does not depend on the daemon.
  * The beacon system user (home /var/lib/beacond, shell /usr/sbin/nologin)
    and /var/log/beacond are created via sysusers.d/tmpfiles.d, wired into
    debian/rules explicitly since dh_installsysusers is not auto-sequenced
    at debhelper compat 13.
  * /etc/profile.d/beacon-env.sh is shipped as a symlink to
    /usr/lib/beacond/beacon-env.sh rather than as a plain file: it is code,
    not site configuration, and dpkg treats every plain file under /etc as a
    conffile by default. A symlink is never a conffile, so upgrades always
    replace its target and fixes always land. Site overrides belong in
    /etc/beacon/beacon-site.sh, which the script sources if present.
  * beacond.service is left at debhelper's default policy (enable + start on
    install, restart on upgrade): the packaged config already matches the
    daemon's built-in defaults and it depends on nothing external, unlike a
    service that needs site config or another host before it can run.

 -- beacond maintainers <beacond@example.com>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
